---
// ABOUTME: /services/ — the few outside engagements Esteban takes on alongside his Peec AI role: fractional CTO, software development, leadership coaching, SOC 2 / ISO 27001 groundwork.
// ABOUTME: Deliberately not in the header nav; linked from About, the footer and llms.txt. Every claim here is sourced from the CV, About page, portfolio or public GitHub repos.

import BaseLayout from '../layouts/BaseLayout.astro';
---

<BaseLayout
  title="Services"
  description="Fractional CTO work, software development, engineering leadership coaching and SOC 2 / ISO 27001 groundwork, alongside my role at Peec AI, so availability is limited."
>
  <article class="services-page">
    <header class="services-page__header reveal">
      <h1 class="services-page__title">Services</h1>
      <p class="services-page__lede">
        I work full-time as an Engineering Manager at <a href="https://peec.ai">Peec AI</a>.
        Alongside that I take on a small number of outside engagements, where 15+ years in tech and
        7+ years of managing engineering teams can be useful to someone else. Availability is
        limited, so the best first step is an email describing where you are.
      </p>
    </header>

    <div class="prose services-page__prose reveal">
      <section aria-labelledby="fractional-cto">
        <h2 id="fractional-cto">Fractional CTO</h2>
        <p class="services-page__problem">
          Your company needs senior technical direction, but not a full-time hire.
        </p>
        <p>
          I help with the decisions a CTO would own: how the platform is built, how the engineering
          team is organised, how delivery is measured, and what to fix first. That's the work I've
          done in-house: leading platform engineering for 60+ product engineers at Zenjob, running
          the Supply vertical there (3 engineering managers, 30+ engineers), and introducing
          DORA-aligned metrics across the organisation. Time commitment and format are agreed per
          engagement.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="software-development">
        <h2 id="software-development">Software development</h2>
        <p class="services-page__problem">
          You need something built, whether a product, an internal tool or an AI feature, and your
          team doesn't have room for it.
        </p>
        <p>
          I haven't stopped coding. On the side I've built and run
          <a href="https://quik.so">Quik</a>, an AI agent platform in Go (gRPC, NATS JetStream, an
          embeddings pipeline, and agent loops with tool calling), and
          <a href="https://bluetip.ai">BlueTip</a>, an AI writing platform in Next.js and TypeScript
          with multi-provider LLM integration and Stripe. Smaller things live on
          <a href="https://github.com/esttorhe">GitHub</a>: Obsidian plugins, a Raycast extension, a
          native macOS menu bar app in Swift, and tools in Go like
          <a href="https://github.com/esttorhe/blogwatcher-ui">blogwatcher-ui</a>. Before management
          I spent a decade as an iOS engineer. With limited time, this works best for well-scoped
          builds.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="coaching">
        <h2 id="coaching">Engineering leadership coaching</h2>
        <p class="services-page__problem">
          You've just become a head of engineering, an engineering manager or a tech lead, and the
          job changed under you.
        </p>
        <p>
          I made that move myself, from iOS engineer to engineering manager to head of engineering,
          and I've coached engineers from mid-level to senior at SoundCloud and Zenjob. The
          day-to-day goes from "I have no idea what I'm doing" to "I have no idea what I'm doing,
          but I've seen this before". Coaching is about getting you to the second one faster,
          working on the situations actually in front of you.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="compliance">
        <h2 id="compliance">SOC 2 and ISO 27001 groundwork</h2>
        <p class="services-page__problem">
          You need to get ready for an audit, and nobody on the team has done it before.
        </p>
        <p>
          At Peec AI I help write the security policies, implement the commitments they make, and
          set up the processes that keep them true. I can help you do the same groundwork. The audit
          itself is done by an independent auditor or certification body; I don't certify anyone.
        </p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="how-it-starts">
        <h2 id="how-it-starts">How it starts</h2>
        <ol>
          <li>You email me what's going on and what you're hoping to change.</li>
          <li>
            We have a short call to see whether I'm the right fit, and whether I have the time.
          </li>
          <li>We agree the scope and format in writing before anything starts.</li>
        </ol>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="background">
        <h2 id="background">Background</h2>
        <ul>
          <li>15+ years in tech, 7+ years managing engineering teams.</li>
          <li>
            Led platform engineering at Zenjob, supporting 60+ product engineers on infrastructure,
            observability and developer tooling; improved CI/CD pipeline stability by over 50%.
          </li>
          <li>
            Led the Supply vertical at Zenjob (3 engineering managers, 30+ engineers) through a
            company-wide migration from native iOS and Android to React Native.
          </li>
          <li>
            Led a distributed team at Spotify (8 engineers, grown to 12) building Backstage, and
            defined its plugin marketplace architecture.
          </li>
          <li>
            Led the teams at SoundCloud owning JVMKit, the shared platform behind 200+
            microservices.
          </li>
        </ul>
        <p>The full history is in the <a href="/cv/">CV</a>.</p>
      </section>

      <section aria-labelledby="questions">
        <h2 id="questions">Questions</h2>
        <h3>Is this alongside your job at Peec AI?</h3>
        <p>
          Yes. That's why availability is limited, and why I only take on a few engagements at a
          time.
        </p>
        <h3>What does it cost?</h3>
        <p>It depends on scope. I'll quote once we've talked through what you need.</p>
        <h3>Fractional CTO or coaching?</h3>
        <p>
          Fractional CTO work means I help make and carry technical decisions with your team.
          Coaching means you make them, and I help you get better at it.
        </p>
      </section>

      <p class="services-page__contact">
        <strong>Get in touch</strong>: email me at
        <a href="mailto:me@estebantorr.es">me@estebantorr.es</a>.
      </p>
    </div>
  </article>
</BaseLayout>

<style>
  .services-page {
    max-width: var(--max-content);
    margin: 0 auto;
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
  }

  .services-page__header {
    max-width: var(--measure);
    margin-bottom: var(--space-lg);
  }

  .services-page__title {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 700;
    font-size: var(--text-h1);
    line-height: 1.05;
    letter-spacing: -0.025em;
    color: var(--ink);
    margin: 0 0 var(--space-md);
    text-wrap: balance;
  }

  .services-page__lede {
    font-family: var(--font-prose);
    font-size: var(--text-lead);
    line-height: 1.5;
    color: var(--ink-muted);
    margin: 0;
    text-wrap: pretty;
  }

  .services-page__prose {
    max-width: var(--measure);
  }

  .services-page__prose section + section {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
  }

  /* The buyer's problem leads each offer, set apart from the explanation. */
  .services-page__problem {
    font-style: italic;
    color: var(--ink);
  }

  .services-page__contact {
    margin-top: var(--space-xl);
    padding-top: var(--space-md);
    border-top: 1px solid var(--rule);
  }

  .services-page__contact :global(strong) {
    font-family: var(--font-display);
    font-weight: 600;
  }
</style>
